  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The Stock page has a \"Stock axis\" choice: Along Z (default), Along X, Along Y and Custom. Custom shows three angles in degrees: turn about Z (yaw), tilt about Y (pitch), tilt about X (roll). The choice applies to a box and to a cylinder. The old \"Rotation (yaw deg)\" row is replaced.\n- The turn is stored in the stock's existing `Location.rot`. There is no new shape field and no project-file version step.\n- Apply sends the whole turn through the undoable `SetStock` (new UI queue entry `CommandKind::SetStockPose`; the old `CommandKind::SetStock { yaw_deg }` stays for its callers). Undo restores the old turn.\n- The page reads a stored turn back. A preset turn shows its preset. Any other turn shows Custom with its angles (`camcraft_geometry::geometry::stock_axis`).\n- Before any simulation, the page shows a plain note when the simulation cannot cut the drafted stock: a stock tilted off the axes. Since #2758 the simulation cuts a cylinder laid along X or Y. The note asks the simulation's own law (`stock_follow::sim_frame`). The refusals `OBLIQUE_STOCK` and `LAID_CYLINDER` do not change. A box laid along X or Y is a square turn, so the simulation cuts it and no note shows.\n- MCP `set_stock` takes an optional `axis` (\"z\", \"x\", \"y\") or `angles_deg` ({yaw, pitch, roll}), not both. It calls the same `SetStock` and returns `{ stock, axis, angles_deg }`. The camcraft-mcp skill row is updated.\n- `sketch.rs`: the DXF profile face ignored the stock's turn. Now an upright stock keeps its top face, a stock laid square is read as the same solid unturned, and a laid cylinder or a tilted stock is refused by name (`sketch::NO_TOP_FACE`). `ImportDxf` shows that refusal.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2576-stock-axis.md`.\n- Follow-up: #2758 (stock simulation: cut a cylinder or box stock that lies along X or Y).\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## Readings\n\n- X preset = a quarter turn about Y (stock Z goes to world +X). Y preset = a minus quarter turn about X (stock Z goes to world +Y).\n- A laid 50 x 40 x 20 box at (3, 4, 5): the profile face is at the highest Z of the turned box, and its normal is world +Z (pinned).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/stock_axis.rs`:\n  - `set_stock_lays_a_cylinder_along_x_and_undo_restores_the_old_turn`\n  - `a_turned_stock_survives_the_project_file`\n  - `mcp_set_stock_takes_an_axis_and_undo_walks_it_back`\n  - `a_profile_lies_on_a_laid_box_and_a_laid_cylinder_is_refused`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/stock_axis.rs`:\n  - `the_stock_page_offers_the_stock_axis_and_custom_angles`\n  - `apply_lays_the_stock_along_x_and_undo_stands_it_up_again`\n  - `a_custom_turn_reads_back_with_its_angles`\n  - `a_laid_stock_shows_no_simulation_note_and_a_tilted_one_does`\n- `fit_to_models_wraps_the_part_in_a_laid_stocks_frame` (Fit to Models on a laid stock fits in the frame of the stock)\n- `layout_page_stock` now has the \"Stock axis\" anchor.\n- `camcraft-geometry` unit tests: `each_preset_carries_the_stock_axis_onto_its_world_axis`, `custom_angles_read_back_and_a_bad_angle_is_refused`.\n- The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up by 4. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe gate is on ee65e8666. The PR comment of the review fix has the details.\n- Quick gate on b44e15628: 1038 steps. The 2 red steps (`stock_axis`, `mcp_doc_drift`) came from main (#2758 and the tool reference doc). Both are fixed in ee65e8666, and those suites and the sketch suites pass there.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: 1388 passed, 0 failed.\n- Clippy `-D warnings` on `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: 234 reached (197 app, 37 motion). Not run. The cut gate covers them.\n- New pinning test: `fit_to_models_wraps_the_part_in_a_laid_stocks_frame`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe pictures are renders of the real shell through the egui_kittest renderer (the same frame code), with the seeded test document and a 40 x 100 cylinder. They are not captures of a live app window.\n\nBefore (main):\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/screenshots/issue-2576/stock-before.png)\n\nAfter, Along Z:\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/screenshots/issue-2576/stock-after.png)\n\nAfter, Along Y (the simulation note shows):\n\n![after along Y](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/screenshots/issue-2576/stock-after-along-y.png)\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The live GUI viewport draw of a laid stock (the viewport already draws `Location.rot`; not changed here).\n- A simulation of a laid box through the GUI (the sim law is unchanged and has its own tests).\n- A DXF import through the GUI on a laid box (the command is pinned headless).\n\nChangelog: The Stock page sets the stock axis (along Z, X or Y, or a custom turn) for a box or a cylinder, and says before a simulation when the simulation cannot cut that stock; MCP `set_stock` takes `axis` or `angles_deg` (#2576)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2576\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
